{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `R`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `R_safestan_copy`, a deterministic copy of `R`, because the original model uses `R` in `transformed data` and `generated quantities` before/away from the SafeStan observation point. Those uses now read the copy, while the protected variable `R` is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. Added `theta ~ uniform(0, theta_max);` to make the finite bounded implicit prior on `theta` explicit for SafeStan's unique-prior requirement. In `data_safe.json`, `R_safestan_copy` is exactly equal to `R` from the supplied data.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // marked
  int<lower=0> C; // captured
  int<lower=0, upper=min(M, C)> R; // recaptured
  int<lower=0, upper=min(M, C)> R_safestan_copy; // deterministic copy of R
}
transformed data {
  real theta_max;
  theta_max = M;
  theta_max = theta_max / (C - R_safestan_copy + M);
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0, upper=theta_max> theta; // proportion marked
}
model {
  theta ~ uniform(0, theta_max);
  R ~ binomial(C, theta);
}
generated quantities {
  real<lower=(C - R_safestan_copy + M)> N; // population
  N = M / theta;
}
","data_safe_json":"{"C":3,"M":3,"R":0,"R_safestan_copy":0}","protected_variables":["R"]}
